# Input for requirements-lock.txt: the exact CPU environment CI installs, pinned to this rig's own
# versions so CI tests what the rig runs. Regenerate with the command in the lock's header (uv;
# `pip install uv` anywhere). uv keeps the lock's current pins where they still fit, so a
# regenerate after editing requirements.txt moves only what has to move.
#
# The torch version here is the one setup.bat / setup.sh install on every path (cu130, cu126,
# CPU, macOS) -- bump them together.
#
# No --generate-hashes: the hashes would have to cover every platform's torch wheel from a second
# index, and Linux CI swaps in headless OpenCV after the install, which would need a hashed file
# of its own. Exact pins already stop a new (e.g. hijacked) release from sneaking in, and PyPI
# never lets a published file be replaced in place.
-r requirements.txt
torch==2.12.0
torchvision==0.27.0
